#. Tag: title
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sharing data with &kontact; via <acronym>IMAP</acronym>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For my small office, I was looking for a long time for a <acronym>PIM</"
"acronym> solution that let me share data, so my secretary and I can share "
"contacts, appointments and so on. Being a &kde; user, I've heard about the "
"Kroupware project and wait its completion. But when I saw how complicated is "
"the architecture and setup of the <application>Kolab</application> server "
"1.0 (the server side of the project), I gave up, waiting for an easier to "
"deploy <application>Kolab</application> 2.0. In any case, the "
"<application>Kolab</application> stuff was clearly too much for my needs. "
"Fortunately in the &kde; wiki I've found some piece of <acronym>IRC</"
"acronym> conversation where they were talking about sharing data without the "
"<application>Kolab</application> infrastructure... mmm so interesting!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For small offices and needs, you can have &kontact; use shared data without "
"the need of installing the <application>Kolab</application> server or "
"another groupware backend. It can work with just an <acronym>IMAP</acronym> "
"server, that can be easily set up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"My scenario is a server with Debian unstable and &kde; 3.4. I access "
"&kontact; and other fabulous GNU/Linux apps from windows using Cygwin/X, "
"while waiting Wine project to be able to run the last Windows programs I "
"need (and that are not available under GNU/Linux). I want to share contacts, "
"events, todo, notes with my secretary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is <acronym>IMAP</acronym>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This definition is from the <ulink url=\"http://computeruser.com"
"\">ComputerUser.com High-Tech Dictionary:</ulink> <blockquote><para>Internet "
"Message Access Protocol. A protocol that allows a user to perform certain "
"electronic mail functions on a remote server rather than on a local "
"computer. Through IMAP the user can create, delete, or rename mailboxes; get "
"new messages; delete messages; and perform search functions on mail. A "
"separate protocol is required for sending mail. Also called Internet Mail "
"Access Protocol.</para></blockquote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"So it can be considered a data storage. To use it you you need an "
"<acronym>IMAP</acronym> server, such as <application>Cyrus</application>, "
"<application>Courier</application> or <application>UW</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "<application>Kolab</application> or <acronym>IMAP</acronym>?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<application>Kolab</application> brings the ability to share data between "
"different clients. It makes possible for your secretary to use "
"<application>Outlook</application> and you use &kontact;, for instance."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will have a configuration interface which does user management, mail "
"account setup, a central <acronym>LDAP</acronym> config data and addressbook "
"server, spam and virus filtering, vacation scripts, free busy list handling, "
"resource handling (rooms, cars), groups, distribution lists, automatic "
"invitation handling, &etc;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"But that can cause initial setup troubles. For a newbie like me it means: a "
"long long frustrating nightmare, and too much complexity to manage once "
"working. So no, thanks, I'll go to simple <acronym>IMAP</acronym>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to set up <acronym>IMAP</acronym> server <application>Cyrus</application>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"My choice is <application>Cyrus</application>, that is part of the "
"<application>Kolab</application> set of software, so if l will go for "
"<application>Kolab</application> in the future, at least I'm acquainted with "
"it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Let's start the installation and the setup!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "Become <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# <userinput><command>apt-get</command> <command>install</command> cyrus21-"
"imapd cyrus21-common cyrus21-admin cyrus21-client sasl-bin sasl2-bin</"
"userinput> \n"
"<computeroutput>Installing cyrus21-imapd...</"
"computeroutput><lineannotation>The installer asks something I've not "
"understood about an search address... I just pressed <keycap>Enter</keycap></"
"lineannotation>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The installer also created the user <systemitem class=\"username\">cyrus</"
"systemitem> that is in the (automatically created) group <systemitem class="
"\"groupname\">sasl</systemitem>, that is the <quote>owner</quote> of all "
"cyrus files. At the end with <command>ps <option>-A</option></command> you "
"can find the new processes: <command>cyrmaster</command> and "
"<command>notifyd</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The real problem in setting up <application>Cyrus</application> is the "
"authentication, just because it's not trivial and I'm a newbie, with limited "
"knowledge about what I'm doing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<application>Cyrus</application> can use different <acronym>SASL</acronym> "
"(Simple Authentication and Security Layer) mechanisms, the default being "
"sasldb (it stores usernames and passwords in the SASL secrets file "
"<filename>sasldb</filename>), but also getpwent, kerberos4, kerberos5, PAM, "
"rimap, shadow and LDAP are supported."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since I don't want to define users/passwords different than the ones that "
"access my &Linux; box I choose then <quote>shadow</quote> mechanism so "
"<application>Cyrus</application> will use &Linux; passwords for authenticate."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To do so we have to tell sasl to use <command>saslauthd</command> as "
"password authentication method, and then setup <command>saslauthd</command> "
"to use <quote>shadow</quote> (or <quote>getpwent</quote>) as the "
"authentication mechanism."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "OK, let's start!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>, change the Linux "
"password of <systemitem class=\"username\">cyrus</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "# <userinput><command>passwd <option>cyrus</option></command></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the password you like (and you will remember) we will use for this "
"example <quote>cyrus</quote> as the <application>cyrus</application> "
"administrator password."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "# <command>vi</command> <filename>/etc/imapd.conf</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"sasl_pwcheck_method: <userinput>saslauthd</userinput> "
"<lineannotation>instead of the default <literal>auxprop</literal></"
"lineannotation>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "remove the <literal>#</literal> remark from the line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "#admins: cyrus"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"this way you can administer <application>cyrus</application> logging in as "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">cyrus</systemitem> user (what a fantasy I "
"have!)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# <userinput><command>vi</command> <filename>/etc/default/saslauthd</"
"filename></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "Uncomment the line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "# START=yes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(otherwise the <application>saslauthd</application> will not start at boot "
"time, even if referenced in some <filename class=\"directory\">/etc/rcx.d</"
"filename>!)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"and instead of <literal>MECHANISMS=\"pam\"</literal> put "
"<userinput>MECHANISMS=\"shadow\"</userinput> this way at the boot a "
"<command>saslauthd</command> <option>-a <parameter>shadow</parameter></"
"option> will be executed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once exited from your editor, restart <application>sasl</application> and "
"<application>cyrus</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "To test <acronym>IMAP</acronym>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>su</command> <option>cyrus</option></userinput>\n"
"$ <userinput><command>imtest</command> <option>-m login -p imap localhost</"
"option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You are prompted for the <systemitem class=\"username\">cyrus</systemitem> "
"(user) password, so enter it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the user <systemitem class=\"username\">cyrus</systemitem> is correctly "
"authenticated, the following lines will appear:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<computeroutput>S: L01 OK User logged in\n"
"Authenticated.</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To exit type <userinput>. logout</userinput> (&ie; dot space <quote>logout</"
"quote>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now add a user named <systemitem class=\"username\">groupware</systemitem> "
"and set a password for it, using your usual system tools. It should be in an "
"unprivileged group such as <systemitem class=\"groupname\">nobody</"
"systemitem> and does not require a login shell or a home directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now I have to create the user and an <acronym>IMAP</acronym> in "
"<application>cyrus</application> also:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# <userinput><command>cyradm</command> <option>--user cyrus localhost</"
"option></userinput>\n"
"after entering the password for the admin user <systemitem class=\"username"
"\">cyrus</systemitem>, you get the prompt <prompt>localhost&gt;</prompt>\n"
"<prompt>localhost&gt;</prompt> <userinput><command>cm</command> <option>user."
"groupware</option></userinput>\n"
"<prompt>localhost&gt;</prompt> <userinput><command>lm</command></userinput> "
"<lineannotation>lists the mailbox only just created</lineannotation>\n"
"<computeroutput>user.groupware (\\HasNoChildren))</computeroutput>\n"
"<prompt>localhost&gt;</prompt> <userinput><command>quit</command></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can type <userinput><command>help</command></userinput> for a list of "
"available commands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can check what has happened with:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# <userinput><command>ls</command> <option>-l</option> <filename class="
"\"directory\">/var/spool/cyrus/mail/g/user/groupware</filename></userinput>\n"
"<computeroutput>total 12\n"
"-rw------- 1 cyrus mail          4 Oct 29 20:55 cyrus.cache\n"
"-rw------- 1 cyrus mail 155 Oct 29 20:55 cyrus.header\n"
"-rw------- 1 cyrus mail 76 Oct 29 20:55 cyrus.index</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now you should be able to connect with an <acronym>IMAP</acronym> client as "
"the <systemitem class=\"username\">groupware</systemitem> user and see the "
"<literal>INBOX</literal>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <acronym>IMAP</acronym> protocol, selecting the mailbox "
"<literal>INBOX</literal> is a magic word, a sort of <quote>alias</quote> for "
"the above directory structure. The client sees <literal>INBOX</literal>, and "
"the <acronym>IMAP</acronym> server maps it in the <filename class=\"directory"
"\">/var/spool/cyrus/mail/...</filename> folder and file structure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to setup &kontact; clients"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I connect to my GNU/Linux office server PC (a sort of \"black box\" without "
"monitor and keyboard) from 2 &Windows; 2000 PC with <application>Cygwin/X</"
"application>, using them as a X-Window server (in the near future I hope to "
"replace both with 2 mini-itx thin clients using the LTSP). With this setup "
"every user runs &kontact; on the same machine where <application>Cyrus</"
"application> is installed and running (localhost)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To have &kontact; work with <acronym>IMAP</acronym>, there are these steps "
"to complete:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create an <acronym>IMAP</acronym> account on the <application>Cyrus</"
"application> for fake <systemitem class=\"username\">groupware</systemitem> "
"user (already previously done!)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create/configure an <acronym>IMAP</acronym> account in &kmail; for login as "
"that user"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use kresources to make &kontact; components work with data taken from "
"<acronym>IMAP</acronym> source"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enable groupware functionality and make related subfolders of that "
"<acronym>IMAP</acronym> <literal>INBOX</literal> (if not already)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enjoy &kontact; and shared data through <application>Cyrus</application> IMAP"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"So login to &kde; with the first <quote>real user</quote> account you want "
"to provide groupware functionality to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "Let's create the IMAP account in &kmail;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Run &kontact; and select <guilabel>Mail</guilabel> (the &kmail; component). "
"From the menu choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure KMail </guimenuitem><guilabel>Accounts</"
"guilabel><guilabel>Receiving</guilabel></menuchoice> tab, press the "
"<guibutton>Add...</guibutton> button. You will then be prompted for the type "
"of your email account, and select <guilabel>disconnected IMAP</guilabel> "
"(not just <guilabel>IMAP</guilabel>). Then in the <guilabel>General</"
"guilabel> tab enter the following data:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Account Name:</guilabel> <userinput>office_gwdata</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A name that will be used for the <quote>local</quote> folder that points to "
"this <acronym>IMAP</acronym> account."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Login:</guilabel> <userinput>groupware</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:271
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <application>Cyrus</application> user we have chosen as <quote>owner</"
"quote> of all of the office data"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "Password:"
msgstr "Mot de pas :"

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The password of the <systemitem class=\"username\">groupware</systemitem> "
"user."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Host:</guilabel> <userinput>localhost</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remember for our example, the &kontact; client runs on the same computer as "
"the <acronym>IMAP</acronym> server"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Port:</guilabel> <userinput>143</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid "The default"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check <guilabel>store IMAP password</guilabel> so you will not be asked for "
"it next time you run &kontact;. Check the <guilabel>Enable interval mail "
"checking</guilabel> and set a value in minutes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that we have checked the <guilabel>disconnected IMAP</guilabel> type "
"account. This has the effect that a copy of the groupware data is stored "
"<quote>locally</quote> to the client (under the home folder), and it is "
"synchronized every time the client connects. This seems very inefficient, "
"since your data is duplicated many times (&ie; if you have 10 users that use "
"&kontact;, you have 10+1 times the data), but it is the only way to make "
"things run fast, because at every connection &kontact; has to fetch all data "
"and have &korganizer; and &kaddressbook; interpret it. If you use "
"<quote>disconnected IMAP</quote> data is cached locally, and only the "
"<quote>delta</quote> (&ie; the data that has changed) is sent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the other end, if your users run &korganizer; on the same PC that runs "
"the <acronym>IMAP</acronym> server, it seems reasonable to use "
"<acronym>IMAP</acronym> (that is called <quote>online IMAP</quote>) to save "
"space, since transfer speed should not be an issue. But unfortunately this "
"does not work because &kontact; does not update automatically the "
"<guilabel>Calendar</guilabel> folder in <quote>online IMAP</quote>, so you "
"are not updated when someone adds events (you must manually switch to "
"&kmail; application and click on the <guilabel>Calendar</guilabel> folder). "
"In addition, at start up when it does read <guilabel>Calendar</guilabel> "
"folders, you may see a tremendous flicker and slow data updates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now we have to tell &kontact; to use <acronym>IMAP</acronym> as the data "
"source for its various components. From the &kmenu;, choose <guimenuitem>Run "
"command</guimenuitem>, run <userinput><command>kcmshell kresources</"
"command></userinput>. In the combo box select <guilabel>Contacts</guilabel>, "
"then press the <guibutton>Add...</guibutton> button, and choose "
"<guilabel>Addressbook on IMAP Server via KMail</guilabel>. Then select that "
"new line and press <guibutton>Use as Standard</guibutton> button. Do the "
"same for <guilabel>Calendar</guilabel> and <guilabel>Notes</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now we have to enable the &kmail; (and as a consequence, the whole "
"&kontact;) groupware functionality:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose from the menu <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure KMail</guimenuitem><guilabel>Misc</"
"guilabel><guilabel>Groupware</guilabel></menuchoice>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "Check <guilabel>Enable IMAP resource functionality</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose <guilabel>English</guilabel> as <guilabel>Language of the groupware "
"folders</guilabel> (this is in case you already have the folders in the "
"<acronym>IMAP</acronym> server created by a different program in a different "
"language)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now move to <guilabel>Resource folder are in account</guilabel> and select "
"the the <guilabel>Inbox</guilabel> subfolder of the <guilabel>office_gwdata</"
"guilabel> folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Leave <guilabel>Hide groupware folders</guilabel> unchecked for now, so we "
"can see that happens. You can return here and check it once everything is "
"clear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you press OK you are prompted with: <computeroutput>&kmail; will now "
"create the required folders for the IMAP resource as subfolders of Inbox</"
"computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you do not want this, press <guibutton>No</guibutton>, and the "
"<acronym>IMAP</acronym> resource will be disabled. Press <guibutton>Yes</"
"guibutton> (this happens only the first time with the first <quote>real "
"user</quote>). You will immediately see that in the &kmail; folder tree, "
"under <menuchoice><guilabel>office_gwdata</guilabel><guilabel>Inbox</"
"guilabel></menuchoice> these subfolders are created:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid "Calendar"
msgstr "Calendièr"

#. Tag: member
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:372
#, no-c-format
msgid "Contacts"
msgstr "Contactes"

#. Tag: member
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "Notes"
msgstr "Nòtas"

#. Tag: member
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tasks"
msgstr "Prètzfaches"

#. Tag: member
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid "Journal"
msgstr "Jornal"

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid "if you now do a:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# <command>ls</command> <option>-l /var/spool/cyrus/mail/g/user/groupware/</"
"option>\n"
"<computeroutput>drwx------ 2 cyrus mail 144 Oct 31 16:36 Calendar\n"
"drwx------ 2 cyrus mail 144 Oct 31 16:36 Contacts\n"
"drwx------ 2 cyrus mail 144 Oct 31 16:36 Journal\n"
"drwx------ 2 cyrus mail 144 Oct 31 16:36 Notes\n"
"drwx------ 2 cyrus mail 144 Oct 31 16:36 Tasks\n"
"-rw------- 1 cyrus mail      4 Oct 31 15:28 cyrus.cache\n"
"-rw------- 1 cyrus mail 155 Oct 29 20:55 cyrus.header\n"
"-rw------- 1 cyrus mail 76 Oct 31 15:28 cyrus.index</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you see, the <guilabel>office_gwdata Inbox</guilabel> is stored not local "
"to the &kontact; current user home, but in the <acronym>IMAP</acronym> "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">groupware</systemitem> user's folders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now &kontact; is ready to work and store data there. In the calendar "
"application, if &kmail; <acronym>IMAP</acronym> account was of type "
"<quote>disconnected</quote>, the <guilabel>resource</guilabel> window should "
"display the item <guilabel>Imap resource</guilabel> with 3 subitems, that "
"are paths to local home files. Instead, the <guilabel>Contacts</guilabel> "
"application does not show subitems below the <guilabel>Imap resource</"
"guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can now login to &kde; with a different username and set up his/her "
"&kontact; client in a very similar manner:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Open &kontact; and in the <guilabel>Mail</guilabel> component add an "
"<acronym>IMAP</acronym> account specifying as <guilabel>host</guilabel> the "
"computer where <application>Cyrus</application> server runs (in my case: "
"<literal>192.168.1.3</literal>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remember to check the <guilabel>Enable interval mail checking</guilabel> and "
"set a value in minutes. When you confirm, you are not prompted for the "
"subfolder creation (since they are found in the <acronym>IMAP</acronym> "
"server), and you see them in the folder tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Activate the groupware functionality to be able to save data in the "
"<acronym>IMAP</acronym> server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Beware that in <quote>disconnected <acronym>IMAP</acronym></quote>, data are "
"transmitted from a client to <acronym>IMAP</acronym> server only when the "
"clients connects to check for new mail. So if you have your &kontact; "
"clients with an <guilabel>interval mail checking</guilabel> of, for "
"instance, 5 minutes, in the worst case you have a 10 minutes delay between "
"the event being written and its appearance to the other users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to have Read Only Access"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Beware that I've been confirmed that Notes <acronym>IMAP</acronym> "
"implementation in &kontact; prior to version 1.01 is broken, so this setup "
"will not work for them, so you want to use them, you need to use the "
"previous setup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the previous setup, we have the same <quote>fake</quote> user, named "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">groupware</systemitem>, that is used by all "
"the <quote>real</quote> &kontact; users (&ie; <systemitem class=\"username"
"\">tony</systemitem>, <systemitem class=\"username\">rohn</systemitem>, "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">amanda</systemitem>, &etc;) through the "
"<acronym>IMAP</acronym> account with its login and password. But this way "
"every real user has the same read/write permissions of the others, since "
"everyone connects as the user <systemitem class=\"username\">groupware</"
"systemitem> to the <acronym>IMAP</acronym> server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To limit access to some users (typically, providing read-only access), we "
"can use the <acronym>ACL</acronym> (Access Control Lists)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select in &kmail; a subfolder of <guilabel>office_gwdata</guilabel> inbox, "
"for instance <guilabel>Calendar</guilabel>, and right click the mouse. "
"Select <guilabel>Properties</guilabel><guilabel>Access Control</guilabel> "
"tab. Here you can enter the users you want give access to this folder and "
"what they can do."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Just to experiment trying to exchange events, we give <quote>All</quote> "
"permission to the user <systemitem class=\"username\">mary</systemitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At <application>cyrus</application> level (in the <acronym>PC</acronym> that "
"runs <acronym>IMAP</acronym> server cyrus, with <application>cyrus</"
"application> tools), we first need to add the user <systemitem class="
"\"username\">mary</systemitem>, so it's an <acronym>IMAP</acronym> "
"recognized user, and create an <acronym>IMAP</acronym> folder for her."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then we login to GNU/Linux as <systemitem class=\"username\">mary</"
"systemitem> and enter &kontact;. As previously shown, we will setup an "
"<acronym>IMAP</acronym> account in &kmail; with the same data but the one of "
"the user (instead of the fake user <systemitem class=\"username\">groupware</"
"systemitem> and its password, we will use <systemitem class=\"username"
"\">mary</systemitem> and her password)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &kmail; folder tree, this time you will see this structure: "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>office_gwdata</guimenu><guisubmenu>user</guisubmenu> "
"<guisubmenu>groupware</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Calendar and Tasks</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Check the mail (<menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Check Mail</guimenuitem></menuchoice>) and you will "
"also have an <quote>inbox</quote> folder under <quote>office_gwdata</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now enable &kmail; groupware functionality, and in <guilabel>Resource "
"folders are subfolders of</guilabel> put the <guimenuitem>inbox</"
"guimenuitem> that is subfolder of <quote>office_gwdata</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now enable &kmail; groupware functionality, and in <guilabel>Resource "
"folders are subfolders of</guilabel> put the <guimenuitem>inbox</"
"guimenuitem> that is subfolder of <guisubmenu>office_gwdata</guisubmenu>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now you have two branches of folder under <quote>office_gwdata</quote>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<quote>inbox</quote> with Calendar, Contacts, Notes, Tasks and Journal, that "
"are saved on <systemitem class=\"username\">mary</systemitem> <acronym>IMAP</"
"acronym> folders on the <acronym>IMAP</acronym> server"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<quote>user</quote>, with the subfolder <quote>groupware</quote> and the "
"subfolders to which <systemitem class=\"username\">mary</systemitem> has "
"access to (in this example, Calendar and Tasks)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&RMB; click on the <quote>user</quote> <quote>Calendar</quote> and check if "
"it's of type Calendar (if not, set it to be), and also if <quote>user</"
"quote><quote>Tasks</quote> is of type Tasks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now in Calendar you have two available <acronym>IMAP</acronym> resources to "
"write against, so if you create a new event, you are prompted which one use "
"(or if you left the local resources available, you have 3!)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: groupware-kontact.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You have go to the lower left small window in Calendar, the one that shows "
"available resources, and uncheck the ones that don't point to <guilabel>."
"groupware.directory</guilabel> path (see the tail part of each resource "
"path)."
msgstr ""

